Hi! At IETF 125, the chairs to an action item to update the FATT pages. =
The changes are:

1. Building on Usama's PR - clarify what happened to each I-D; see PR =
#16 [1].
2. Noting that the FATT will not perform cryptanalysis; see Issue #19 =
[2].

To provide a little context on #1, there is no date when the FATT =
process kicked in. We arbitrarily picked early March 2024 as the date =
when it "started" only because that's when Deirdre first suggested it; =
see [3].

As we have noted numerous times, developing a process on the fly and =
applying it to I-Ds at various stages in the WG process has been messy - =
and we did not apply the process uniformly. Again - mea culpa. We will =
try to do better going forward.

As far as why the recent crop - and I use the word "recent" liberally - =
of algorithm I-Ds that did not go through the FATT, they did not go =
through the FATT because we had some sense that that was not the FATT's =
job though we never really articulated that well. We would like to note =
that none of these recent algorithms I-D went through the FATT starting =
with draft-ietf-tls-deprecate-obsolete-kex, and then =
draft-ietf-tls-hybrid-design, draft-ietf-tls-tls13-pkcs1, =
draft-ietf-ecdhe-mlkem, draft-ietf-tls-mlkem, and draft-ietf-tls-mldsa. =
Maybe a good call on chairs' part maybe not, but that's what happened.

There were other suggestions at IETF 125, but I do not remember much =
support for them.

spt

[1] https://github.com/tlswg/tls-fatt/pull/16/ <-ready to merge
[2] https://github.com/tlswg/tls-fatt/issues/19
[3] =
